# Blossoming Tortoise: "Activated abilities of lands you control cost {1} less to activate" takes exactly one generic mana off (CR 601.2f).
# The milled Drannith Ruins comes back tapped on turn 1 and, untapped on turn 3, puts its counters on the Ornithopter that entered this
# turn for {1} and {T} instead of {2} and {T}: Mox Jet's single mana pays it (nothing is left in the pool; a cost of {T} alone would leave it floating). The
# Ruins cannot pay for itself, tapping as part of the cost.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Blossoming Tortoise
Ornithopter
Island x3
Drannith Ruins
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

